-  {
-   "cell_type": "markdown",
-   "id": "93c6ff51-f4b1-409b-b5a0-4a92c71102bd",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "source": [
-    "### Initialize the store with the template"
-   ]
-  },
-  {
-   "cell_type": "code",
-   "execution_count": 9,
-   "id": "f3fcdade-7ca4-465e-af3c-c7874b372f7a",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "outputs": [],
-   "source": [
-    "import icechunk as ic\n",
-    "\n",
-    "repo = ic.Repository.create(storage)"
-   ]
-  },
-  {
-   "cell_type": "markdown",
-   "id": "ee6353b2-9be5-47d1-a76f-452e92432ecf",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "source": [
-    "We specify important details about how the `lclu` variable is recorded on disk in the `encoding`. Specifically \n",
-    "1. we choose a Zarr chunksize of (1, 1000, 1000) which means each chunk has 1000x1000 spatial fooprint for a single year; Importantly this perfectly subdivides each tile which are 40_000 x 40_000.\n",
-    "2. set the `fill_value` to 255. Empty tiles will be filled with this value. This value was chosen from [the legend](https://storage.googleapis.com/earthenginepartners-hansen/GLCLU2000-2020/legend.xlsx) provided with the dataset."
-   ]
-  },
-  {
-   "cell_type": "code",
-   "execution_count": 10,
-   "id": "e15fa331-8351-4251-948b-56c82608767e",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "outputs": [
-    {
-     "data": {
-      "text/plain": [
-       "'VD9R98Q7DC2Y3HYCPXAG'"
-      ]
-     },
-     "execution_count": 10,
-     "metadata": {},
-     "output_type": "execute_result"
-    }
-   ],
-   "source": [
-    "session = repo.writable_session(\"main\")\n",
-    "template.to_zarr(\n",
-    "    session.store,\n",
-    "    compute=False,  # important, don't write data values, just the array metadata!\n",
-    "    mode=\"w\",\n",
-    "    encoding={\"lclu\": {\"chunks\": ZARR_CHUNK_SIZE, \"fill_value\": 255}},\n",
-    "    consolidated=False,\n",
-    ")\n",
-    "session.commit(\"initialize array\")"
-   ]
-  },
-  {
-   "cell_type": "markdown",
-   "id": "596b02f3-e046-4f9b-97bf-4ba4c9833383",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "source": [
-    "## Write a single tile"
-   ]
-  },
-  {
-   "cell_type": "markdown",
-   "id": "7a3320a7-6c09-4141-a436-3be22218ecfb",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "source": [
-    "A single tile distributed as a single GeoTIFF corresponds to a contiguous \"region\" within the full data cube. \n",
-    "To construct the full datacube, we will\n",
-    "\n",
-    "1. read each available tile, and write to the appropriate region of the data cube.\n",
-    "2. need to determine this region using the tiling grid. \n",
-    "3. use `to_zarr(..., region=...)` to write to that region of the full datacube.\n",
-    "\n",
-    "Helpfully, rioxarray provides a `.rio.bounds` method that lets us access the bounding box for the tile."
-   ]
-  },
-  {
-   "cell_type": "code",
-   "execution_count": null,
-   "id": "a07f0ef8-da71-480f-b79d-6e6f5564ac58",
-   "metadata": {},
-   "outputs": [],
-   "source": [
-    "def update_tile(\n",
-    "    *, session: ic.Session, tiling: TilingGrid, tile: str, year: int\n",
-    ") -> ic.Session:\n",
-    "    \"\"\"\n",
-    "    Read a single tile, and write it to the appropriate region of the Icechunk store using Zarr.\n",
-    "\n",
-    "    Returns the Icechunk session, to allow for coordinated distributed writes. See\n",
-    "    https://icechunk.io/en/latest/parallel/ for more.\n",
-    "    \"\"\"\n",
-    "    tile = read_tile(tile=tile, year=year, chunks=None)\n",
-    "    tile.drop_vars(\"spatial_ref\").to_zarr(\n",
-    "        session.store,\n",
-    "        region=tiling.get_region(tile),\n",
-    "        consolidated=False,\n",
-    "    )\n",
-    "    return session"
-   ]
-  },
