+       "Dimensions:      (year: 1, x: 40000, y: 40000)\n",
+       "Coordinates:\n",
+       "  * year         (year) int64 8B 2000\n",
+       "  * x            (x) float64 320kB -180.0 -180.0 -180.0 ... -170.0 -170.0 -170.0\n",
+       "  * y            (y) float64 320kB 70.0 70.0 70.0 70.0 ... 60.0 60.0 60.0 60.0\n",
+       "    spatial_ref  int64 8B ...\n",
+       "Data variables:\n",
+       "    lclu         (year, y, x) uint8 2GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 8000, 8000), meta=np.ndarray>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 6,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "def read_tile(\n",
+    "    tile: str, year: int, *, chunks=dict(zip((\"band\", \"y\", \"x\"), DASK_CHUNK_SIZE))\n",
+    "):\n",
+    "    \"\"\"\n",
+    "    Helper function to read a single tile, specified as a string e.g. '70N_180W'\n",
+    "    for a single year.\n",
+    "    \"\"\"\n",
+    "    import os\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    # unauthenticated access\n",
+    "    os.environ[\"GS_NO_SIGN_REQUEST\"] = \"1\"\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    from rasterio.env import Env\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    with Env(GDAL_CACHEMAX=0, VSI_CACHE=False, VSI_CACHE_SIZE=0):\n",
+    "        ds = (\n",
+    "            xr.open_dataset(\n",
+    "                f\"{ROOT_URI}/{year}/{tile}.tif\",\n",
+    "                engine=\"rasterio\",\n",
+    "                # we must read as dask array so that the expand_dims step is lazy\n",
+    "                chunks=chunks,\n",
+    "                mask_and_scale=False,\n",
+    "                lock=False,\n",
+    "            )\n",
+    "            # Add a nice data variable name\n",
+    "            .rename({\"band_data\": \"lclu\"})\n",
+    "            # this is a singleton dimension, drop it\n",
+    "            .squeeze(\"band\", drop=True)\n",
+    "            # add a more useful time dimension\n",
+    "            .expand_dims(year=[year])\n",
+    "        )\n",
+    "    return ds\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "ds = read_tile(tile=\"70N_180W\", year=2000)\n",
+    "ds"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "cdeab00b-97b2-4bfd-a3e2-e7dc44caf616",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Create a template for the global datacube\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Now create a \"template\" dataset that represents the full cube. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "The Icechunk store will be initialized with the _structure_ of this dataset, including coordinate labels and metadata but not the actual data values.\n",
+    "1. Since we just need an array of the right shape and data type and the values don't matter, we create a `dask` array of zeros.\n",
+    "2. We assign the `year` coordinate of the right shape.\n",
+    "3. We copy over the `spatial_ref` variable from the tile we opened. It is convention for GDAL to express the affine transformation information as a `GeoTransform` attribute attached to the `spatial_ref` variable. We will rewrite this to be appropriate for the global grid.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Note the chunk size here does not matter; we will explicitly specify the chunking when writing."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 7,
+   "id": "07ec9618-8356-47ae-b2a7-e78d1ef62e62",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/html": [
+       "<pre>&lt;xarray.Dataset&gt; Size: 4TB\n",
+       "Dimensions:      (year: 5, y: 560000, x: 1440000)\n",
+       "Coordinates:\n",
+       "    spatial_ref  int64 8B ...\n",
+       "  * year         (year) int64 40B 2000 2005 2010 2015 2020\n",
+       "Dimensions without coordinates: y, x\n",
+       "Data variables:\n",
+       "    lclu         (year, y, x) uint8 4TB dask.array&lt;chunksize=(5, 560000, 1440000), meta=np.ndarray&gt;\n",
+       "Attributes:\n",
+       "    license:  CC BY 4.0</pre>"
+      ],
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<xarray.Dataset> Size: 4TB\n",
+       "Dimensions:      (year: 5, y: 560000, x: 1440000)\n",
+       "Coordinates:\n",
+       "    spatial_ref  int64 8B ...\n",
+       "  * year         (year) int64 40B 2000 2005 2010 2015 2020\n",
+       "Dimensions without coordinates: y, x\n",
+       "Data variables:\n",
+       "    lclu         (year, y, x) uint8 4TB dask.array<chunksize=(5, 560000, 1440000), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
+       "Attributes:\n",
+       "    license:  CC BY 4.0"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 7,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "template = xr.Dataset(\n",
+    "    {\n",
+    "        \"lclu\": (\n",
+    "            (\"year\", \"y\", \"x\"),\n",
+    "            dask.array.zeros(tiling.datacube_shape, chunks=-1, dtype=np.uint8),\n",
+    "            {\n",
+    "                \"publication\": (\n",
+    "                    \"Potapov, P., Hansen, M.C., Pickens, A., Hernandez-Serna, A., Tyukavina, A., Turubanova, S., Zalles, V., Li, X., Khan, A., Stolle, F. \"\n",
+    "                    \"and Harris, N., 2022. The global 2000-2020 land cover and land use change dataset derived from the Landsat archive: first results. \"\n",
+    "                    \"Front. Remote Sens. 3: 856903.\"\n",
+    "                ),\n",
+    "                \"doi\": \"10.3389/frsen\",\n",
+    "                \"grid_mapping\": \"spatial_ref\",\n",
+    "            },\n",
+    "        )\n",
+    "    },\n",
+    "    coords={\"year\": (\"year\", tiling.year), \"spatial_ref\": ds.spatial_ref},\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "# Update the top-left corner information in the GeoTransform\n",
+    "template.spatial_ref.attrs[\"GeoTransform\"] = (\n",
+    "    f\"{tiling.tilex[0]:.1f} 0.00025 0.0 {tiling.tiley[0]:.1f} 0.0 -0.00025\"\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "template.attrs[\"license\"] = \"CC BY 4.0\"\n",
+    "template"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "93c6ff51-f4b1-409b-b5a0-4a92c71102bd",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Initialize the store with the template"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 9,
+   "id": "f3fcdade-7ca4-465e-af3c-c7874b372f7a",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import icechunk as ic\n",
+    "\n",
+    "repo = ic.Repository.create(storage)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ee6353b2-9be5-47d1-a76f-452e92432ecf",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We specify important details about how the `lclu` variable is recorded on disk in the `encoding`. Specifically \n",
+    "1. we choose a Zarr chunksize of (1, 1000, 1000) which means each chunk has 1000x1000 spatial fooprint for a single year; Importantly this perfectly subdivides each tile which are 40_000 x 40_000.\n",
+    "2. set the `fill_value` to 255. Empty tiles will be filled with this value. This value was chosen from [the legend](https://storage.googleapis.com/earthenginepartners-hansen/GLCLU2000-2020/legend.xlsx) provided with the dataset."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 10,
+   "id": "e15fa331-8351-4251-948b-56c82608767e",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/plain": [
+       "'VD9R98Q7DC2Y3HYCPXAG'"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 10,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "session = repo.writable_session(\"main\")\n",
+    "template.to_zarr(\n",
+    "    session.store,\n",
+    "    compute=False,  # important, don't write data values, just the array metadata!\n",
+    "    mode=\"w\",\n",
+    "    encoding={\"lclu\": {\"chunks\": ZARR_CHUNK_SIZE, \"fill_value\": 255}},\n",
+    "    consolidated=False,\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "session.commit(\"initialize array\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "596b02f3-e046-4f9b-97bf-4ba4c9833383",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Write a single tile"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "7a3320a7-6c09-4141-a436-3be22218ecfb",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "A single tile distributed as a single GeoTIFF corresponds to a contiguous \"region\" within the full data cube. \n",
+    "To construct the full datacube, we will\n",
+    "\n",
+    "1. read each available tile, and write to the appropriate region of the data cube.\n",
+    "2. need to determine this region using the tiling grid. \n",
+    "3. use `to_zarr(..., region=...)` to write to that region of the full datacube.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Helpfully, rioxarray provides a `.rio.bounds` method that lets us access the bounding box for the tile."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "a07f0ef8-da71-480f-b79d-6e6f5564ac58",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "def update_tile(\n",
+    "    *, session: ic.Session, tiling: TilingGrid, tile: str, year: int\n",
+    ") -> ic.Session:\n",
+    "    \"\"\"\n",
+    "    Read a single tile, and write it to the appropriate region of the Icechunk store using Zarr.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    Returns the Icechunk session, to allow for coordinated distributed writes. See\n",
+    "    https://icechunk.io/en/latest/parallel/ for more.\n",
+    "    \"\"\"\n",
+    "    tile = read_tile(tile=tile, year=year, chunks=None)\n",
+    "    tile.drop_vars(\"spatial_ref\").to_zarr(\n",
+    "        session.store,\n",
+    "        region=tiling.get_region(tile),\n",
+    "        consolidated=False,\n",
+    "    )\n",
+    "    return session"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "8c9a337c-bd24-4ea4-9c86-219a65560428",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We will test it out."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 9,
+   "id": "fb342a85-c435-4f0a-9d06-01d29fc93116",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
